will guide them to and through their first internship or first job after graduation. In addition to individual coaching, the Career Center helps students with career exploration, job readiness, graduate school preparation, and employer and alumni networking. Whittier students also benefit from the Career Center's partnerships with employers which provide internships and experiential learning and career treks with industry leaders. The Whittier College Career Center encourages you to begin your career exploration early and remain engaged through every stage of your career development journey. Contact Campus Center, 230 (Second Floor) 562.907.4230 careercenter@whittier.edu Resources Instagram Handshake Job Search Academy Events Latina Leadership Conference Hiring Summits Center for Career and Professional Development Breadcrumb Home / Center for Career and Professional Development Center For Career and Professional Development Expand Center For Career and Professional Development Menu Center For Career and Professional Development Services Handshake Job Search Academy On-Campus Jobs Internships Expand Internships Menu Intex Internship Parker Dewey Micro-Internships Alumni Recruit at Whittier Expand Recruit at Whittier Menu Hiring Guidelines Internship Guidelines Career Toolbox Expand Career Toolbox Menu Career Branding Discover Skills and Interest Resumes & Cover Letters Resources Salary Negotiation Success on the Job Networking & Interviewing Professional Online Communications Professional Image & Etiquette Contact Footer Consumer Information Employment Terms of Use Whittier College is committed to ensuring the accessibility of its web content to people with disabilities. We strive to meet W3C WAI’s Web Content Accessibility Guidelines 2.0, Level AA conformance. To report an accessibility issue, a website problem, or submit feedback, please submit a Website Feedback Form . Copyright © 2026 Whittier College 13406 E. Philadelphia St. Whittier, CA 90602 562.907.4200 Giv